      "The validation observation reports a successful validation result, and activation or reliance follows that success."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The component is activated or relied upon without any preceding validation step.",
      "The validation fails or its result is not interpretable as success.",
      "Only a post-activation inspection is performed, with no pre-activation or pre-reliance check."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "PREDICTS_RESIDUAL_ARTIFACT_INTERFERENCE",
    "definition": "The reasoning predicts that residual state left behind by the agent's own activity will interfere with a later required operation or acceptance condition, and uses that prediction as the reason to remove or reset the residual state before handoff or completion.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The agent text that identifies residual self-created state, predicts its adverse effect on a later operation or acceptance condition, and motivates its removal or reset."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning identifies specific residual state produced by the agent's own activity, such as files, branches, keys, test data, or configuration changes.",
      "The reasoning predicts a concrete adverse consequence for a later operation or acceptance condition, such as a failure, mismatch, or misleading check.",
      "The reasoning treats that prediction as the justification for removing or resetting the identified state before handoff or completion."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning expresses only generic cleanliness or tidiness concerns without a predicted operational consequence.",
      "The predicted consequence concerns state the agent did not create, or state unrelated to its own activity.",
      "The reasoning plans cleanup solely because the state is no longer needed, with no predicted interference with a later operation or acceptance condition."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "ATTRIBUTES_FAILURE_TO_TEST_HARNESS_ARTIFACT",
    "definition": "The reasoning classifies a failure observed during the agent's own verification, probe, or simulated execution as originating in the checking environment — its tooling, missing modules, instrumentation, or simulated conditions — rather than as a defect in the artifact being checked, and treats the artifact's own validity or structure as unaffected.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The agent text that reinterprets the observed failure as originating in the checking environment rather than in the artifact."
      },
      {
        "name": "observation",
        "type": "observation",
        "description": "The observation reporting the failure whose origin is being classified."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The observation reports a failure that occurred during the agent's own verification, probe, or simulation procedure.",
      "The reasoning states that the failure originates in the checking environment, such as missing tooling or modules, test instrumentation, simulated inputs, ad hoc invocation, or missing test-side configuration, rather than in the artifact being checked.",
      "The reasoning treats the artifact's own validity, structure, or behavior as unaffected by that failure, either by affirming this directly or by contrasting the checking conditions with the conditions under which the artifact will actually be used."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning treats the failure as a genuine defect in the delivered artifact, configuration, or state.",
      "The reasoning reports the failure without interpreting where it originated.",
      "The reasoning attributes the failure to the artifact itself or to the conditions under which the artifact will actually be used.",
      "No indication is given that the artifact's own validity is preserved or that the checking conditions differ from actual-use conditions."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "ENUMERATES_REQUIRED_END_STATE",
    "definition": "The reasoning enumerates multiple checkable conditions that the delivered environment must satisfy at handoff, decomposing the final state into individually verifiable invariants rather than listing actions to perform.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The agent text listing the conditions the final environment must satisfy."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning lists multiple distinct conditions the final environment must satisfy, such as services running, repository empty, keys removed, and host entries present.",
      "The listed conditions are phrased as verifiable properties of the resulting state rather than as steps to execute."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning describes a sequence of actions to execute without stating the resulting state conditions.",
      "The reasoning states only a single observation about the current state, with no enumeration of required end-state properties."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "IMPLEMENTS_GUARDED_RECOVERY",
    "definition": "The reasoning establishes that a required capability must survive interruption or restart, and an action creates a repeatable, guard-checked mechanism that restores that capability only when it is absent while avoiding failure or disruptive output, with an observation confirming creation of the mechanism.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "resilience_reasoning",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The agent text identifying the need for the required capability to be restored after restart or interruption."
      },
      {
        "name": "creation_action",
        "type": "action",
        "description": "The action creating the guarded recovery mechanism."
      },
      {
        "name": "creation_result",
        "type": "observation",
        "description": "The observation confirming that the mechanism was created and made usable."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
      "The reasoning frames the mechanism as a safety net keeping a required capability available across restarts, rather than as a one-time start of that capability.",
      "The created mechanism includes a presence check so that an already-running capability is not duplicated or restarted.",
      "The mechanism is specified to fail safely and to avoid output or side effects that disrupt the invoking context.",
      "The observation reports successful creation of the mechanism."
    ],
    "exclusion_conditions": [
      "The mechanism unconditionally starts the capability regardless of whether it is already running.",
