      "The intent is a one-time activation of the capability with no restart or resilience rationale."
    ]
  },
  {
    "name": "RECOVERS_CHECK_WITH_ALTERNATIVE_METHOD",
    "definition": "An executed check fails to yield usable information — because it produced an empty, missing, or unparseable result, or because the tool or command it depends on is unavailable or unsupported — the reasoning attributes that failure to a concrete limitation of the check's method or tooling rather than to the inspected state, and a follow-up action retrieves the intended information using a materially different technique.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "inconclusive_result",
        "type": "observation",
        "description": "The observation reporting the empty, missing, unparseable, or erroring result of the original check, including an error stating that the command or tool the check relies on is unavailable."
      },
      {
        "name": "method_diagnosis",
        "type": "reasoning",
        "description": "The reasoning explaining which property of the check's method or tooling (unsupported syntax, wrong format, an unavailable command, or similar) caused the unusable result."
      },
      {
        "name": "alternative_action",
        "type": "action",
        "description": "The follow-up action that retrieves the intended information through a materially different technique."
      }
    ],
    "assertion_conditions": [
